      "candidate_id": "candidate.stacks.42ab5239b965d3c3c628ed59",
      "label": "lemma-simple-invert",
      "section_ordinal": 27,
      "source_line": 4618,
      "reason": "Pinned modules.tex §27 L4618–4650 item (1) says the images of S become invertible sections of O_X itself. For X a point, O_X=Z, and S={2^n}, this fails. The intended codomain is presumably S^{-1}O_X; source correction or explicit adjudication is required before standalone certification.",
      "packet_path": "harvest/phase2_chat_stage_a/modules/batch_03_sections_21_31/RECONSTRUCTIONS.jsonl"
    },
    {
      "candidate_id": "candidate.stacks.6dab3593549aee4d9a9dd962",
      "label": "lemma-rank",
      "section_ordinal": 14,
      "source_line": 2124,
      "reason": "The source claims the cardinality of every local basis index set equals a value in {0,1,2,...}∪{∞}, although the definition of locally free allows arbitrary cardinalities. Over a point with a field and an uncountably generated free module, the cardinality is an uncountable cardinal, not literally ∞. Clarify whether ∞ denotes every infinite cardinal or change the range and statement.",
      "packet_path": "harvest/phase2_chat_stage_a/modules/batch_02_sections_11_20/RECONSTRUCTIONS.jsonl"
    }
  ],
